<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime"
                    x:Class="AmdNr.App.Languages.Pirate">

  <!-- Pirate English. The same keys as Strings.en.axaml, in its order. -->

  <sys:String x:Key="Str.AppTitle">AMD-NR ReShade Installer</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Subtitle">DLSS 5 neural renderin' on yer Radeon, rigged up for ye</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Games">Plunder</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RemoveGame">Make it walk the plank</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RemoveGameHint">Throws the game off the list, an' Scan the seas passes it by too. Not a file in its hold be touched; Settings hauls it back aboard.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RemovedGame">{0} walked the plank, an' Scan the seas will sail past it. Nothin' in its hold was touched; Settings &gt; Marooned games hauls it back.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RemovedGameInstalled">{0} walked the plank, but the add-on still be stowed in its hold. Haul it back from Settings &gt; Marooned games to scuttle it proper.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.IgnoredGames">Marooned games</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.IgnoredGamesHint">Games ye threw off the list. Scan the seas sails right past 'em, so they stay marooned till ye fetch 'em back from here.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.IgnoredNone">No games marooned, cap'n.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.IgnoredRestore">Haul back aboard</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.IgnoredRestored">{0} be back aboard.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.IgnoredGone">The hold o' {0} sank to the depths, so it only left the marooned games.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NoGames">Empty as a sunk galleon. Add the hold a game or emulator sets sail from.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickFolder">Pick the hold the game sets sail from</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.AddGameMany">Search a hold</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.AddGamePickLibrary">Pick the hold where ye stash yer games</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.AddGameNone">Not a whiff o' anythin' game-like under "{0}".</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset">Heading</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Install">Hoist it</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Uninstall">Scuttle it</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.OpenFolder">Open the hold</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.System">This here vessel</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Gpu">Graphics</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Driver">Driver</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Hip">HIP 7 runtime</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.HipMissing">amdhip64_7.dll be nowhere to be found. On RX 7000 an' RX 9000 a fresh Adrenalin driver carries it aboard; RX 6000 (RDNA2) ships need AMD's HIP SDK 7.2. HIP 6 won't do, matey.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NotRadeon">That don't look like no Radeon. The network sails on RDNA2, RDNA3 an' RDNA4 only.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Ready">Shipshape</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Payloads">Cargo</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Downloading">Haulin' aboard</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Verifying">Checkin' the cargo already in the hold…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PayloadsReady">Hauled aboard an' checked.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManifestLocal">The published cargo manifest couldn't be read, so we be usin' the copy that sails with this app.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManifestFailed">Couldn't read the cargo manifest. Check yer riggin' to the net an' try again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Language">Tongue</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UpdateWorking">Haulin' the update aboard…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Dismiss">Not now, matey</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.LogSaved">The whole ship's log was written next to this app.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Working">Heave ho…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GamesUnreadable">The list o' games couldn't be read. It be stowed as {0} beside it, an' a fresh list started.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CloseWhileBusy">Still scribblin' in a game's hold. Give it a few seconds; close the window once it be done.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.FreeTitle">This be free. If ye paid for it, ye've been plundered.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.FreeBody">Nobody sells any o' this — not the installer, not the add-on, not the runtime, not the weights. If some scallywag charged ye for it, or for a "key" or a "pro version", demand yer doubloons back: what they sold ye be on this page for nothin'.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.OpenSourceBody">It be open source an' it stays that way: read it, change it, build yer own, hand it to yer crew. The one thing we ask be that no scurvy dog turns it into a paid version.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportSection">Toss a doubloon</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportNote">optional, an' it buys ye nothin'</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportKofiTitle">Ko-fi</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportKofiBody">A one-off mug o' coffee (rum not included).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportVakinhaTitle">Vakinha</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportVakinhaBody">The crew's Brazilian treasure chest.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportRail">Support AMD-NR</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportTitle">Keep AMD-NR afloat</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportBody">This ship only stays afloat on the doubloons o' them that sail her. 'Tis two pirates, two graphics cards an' long afternoons o' work: no company, no patron. Everythin' here be free an' stays free. Support unlocks no treasure; it keeps the work sailin'.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupportBrazil">In Brazil, matey? The Vakinha takes Pix, card or boleto.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditRuntimeTitle">DLSS-NR-on-AMD — by danielblnc</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditRuntimeBody">The network itself, an' the reason any o' this sails at all: it be what got DLSS 5's neural renderin' runnin' on Radeon in the first place. The runtime an' weights this app hauls aboard be his work, not ours. Thank ye kindly, danielblnc.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditAddonTitle">dlss5-neural-amd — the add-on</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditAddonBody">What lashes that network to a game through ReShade: the add-on this hoists, an' the releases it lets ye choose from. MIT licensed, an' a separate repository from this installer.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditDiscordTitle">Discord — where the whole crew drinks</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditDiscordBody">New builds, what works in which game, an' where to holler when somethin' breaks.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CreditsSection">The crew</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Scan">Scan the seas</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Scanning">Spyglassin' Steam, Epic, GOG, EA, Ubisoft, Battle.net an' Xbox…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Search">Search the plunder…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Settings">Settings</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.WillDownload">The cargo be hauled aboard an' checked when ye hoist.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NoRoute">Nothin' this game renders with has a heading: the add-on works on D3D11, D3D12, Vulkan an' OpenGL, an' on D3D8, D3D9 an' D3D11 for 32-bit games. A 32-bit OpenGL game, a 64-bit D3D9 one an' a software renderer have none.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchRenderer">This game can sail on {1}. Set it to {0} in its own graphics settings — that be the heading picked here, an' on another API the add-on sees a different game entirely.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchRendererUnreal">This be an Unreal game: add -{0} to its launch options.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CheckWiki">Look this game up on PCGamingWiki</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.EmptyTitle">No plunder yet</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NoMatchTitle">Nary a match</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NoMatch">No game on the list matches "{0}".</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ScanningShort">Spyglassin'…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ScanDone">Scan done: {0} games spotted, {1} new.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstalledBadge">Aboard</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Close">Close</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CloseHint">Close (Esc)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeSection">The game's executable</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeChoose">Choose…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeUseDetected">Use the one we spotted</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNone">No executable in this hold.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNote">The heading be read from this file. If the bitness looks wrong (a launcher up top, the game down in Bin64), point it at the right .exe.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNoteChosen">Ye chose this file yerself, so the lookout leaves it be, even after a rescan.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeNotHere">That file ain't inside this game's hold.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ExeUnreadable">That file ain't a Windows executable this can make sense of.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteMismatch">This heading be for {0} games an' the executable above be {1}. Nothin' stops ye — the lookout may have read the wrong file — but if it read the right one, this won't load.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionSection">Add-on version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxySection">ReShade boards as</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyNote">Automatic uses dxgi.dll, which serves every Direct3D. Change it only if the game refuses to let it aboard.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxySectionOpti">OptiScaler boards as</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyNoteOpti">Automatic uses the first name the OptiScaler wiki gives for this game, or else the one already aboard here, or else dxgi.dll. Pick winmm.dll to leave another program's dxgi.dll be.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyAuto">Automatic</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ProxyAutoWiki">Automatic (wiki: {0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PrefetchAll">Haul it all aboard now</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCache">Swab the cache</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheBody">Throws out the hauled cargo, the covers an' the version list. Nothin' stowed in a game be touched; the next hoist hauls what it needs again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheYes">Swab it</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheYesBody">All of it gets hauled aboard again the next time ye hoist.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ClearCacheNoBody">Leave the cache as it be.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CacheCleared">Cache swabbed — {0} freed.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PayloadsAlreadyThere">Everythin' was already aboard, an' every byte just checked out.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionShipped">bundled</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteShipped">The version this installer set sail with.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteRelease">From the v{0} release on GitHub, checked against its hashes.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionSectionOpti">OptiScaler version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteOpti">OptiScaler {0}, from its GitHub release, every file checked against its hash.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteOptiLmxxf">Carries the lmxxf weights (about 590 MB, RDNA4 only).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.VersionNoteOptiMochizuki">Can bring mochizuki aboard too: see NR runtime.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiSection">NR runtime</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiCheck">Hoist mochizuki too, as a second NR runtime (experimental)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiNote">The DLSS 5 network ported to Vulkan by mochizuki0323. RDNA4 only: RX 9000 series, AMD driver 25.10 or newer. It adds MochizukiNrRuntime.dll an' a dlssnr-amd folder with its model, about 141 MB to haul aboard. danielblnc stays the NR runtime: to use mochizuki, pick it under NR runtime in OptiScaler's Neural tab an' restart the game. The first start in each game compiles the network for a few seconds. Unticked, the next hoist throws out what this app stowed of it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiCheckAddon">Hoist mochizuki too, as a second NR runtime (experimental)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiNoteAddon">The DLSS 5 network ported to Vulkan by mochizuki0323, which the add-on can run instead o' danielblnc's from v0.6.8 on. RDNA4 only: RX 9000 series, AMD driver 25.10 or newer. It adds MochizukiNrRuntime.dll an' a dlssnr-amd folder with its model, about 141 MB to haul aboard. To use it, pick mochizuki (Vulkan) under NR runtime in the add-on's panel an' restart the game. The first start in each game compiles the network for up to a minute. Unticked, the next hoist throws out what this app stowed of it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiNotRdna4">Not on offer for this card ({0}): mochizuki needs the FP8 matrix instructions o' RDNA4, the RX 9000 series.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.MochizukiUnknownGpu">This app couldn't tell which card this be; on anythin' but an RX 9000 series card, mochizuki stays off in game.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickRouteTitle">Pick a heading to hoist with</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickRouteBody">This app couldn't tell which graphics API {0} renders with, so it won't pick a heading for ye. OptiScaler be the one for a D3D12 game that offers DLSS, FSR or XeSS in its settings; ReShade, on D3D11 or D3D12, be the one for any other. The Hoist it button waits till ye pick.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PickRouteDetail">The graphics API be a mystery, so the heading be yers to pick below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterTitle">danielblnc's runtime</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterChoose">Which runtime build goes into this game. The glowin' card be the one in use.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterDownloadTitle">Public Release ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterDownloadBody">Hauled aboard an' checked by this app.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterBuildTitle">Local Supporter Build ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPick">Choose me version.dll or setup…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPickOther">Choose another file…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPitch">Newer than the Public Release, from yer own version.dll or danielblnc's setup.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPitch.0.5.0">0.5.0 adds kernels for RDNA3 cards.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPitch.0.6.0">0.6.0 welcomes RX 6000 (RDNA2) cards aboard, which be needin' AMD's HIP SDK 7.2, an' stops the flickerin' in dark corners an' on wee lights.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterNotDistributed">Never hauled nor shared by this app. Yer file be checked by SHA-256 an' kept, so other games don't ask again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUse">Use me supporter files…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUseDownload">Public Release</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterPickTitle">Yer version.dll or dlssnr_on_amd_setup.exe</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterFiles">version.dll, dlssnr_on_amd_setup.exe</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterAnyFile">Any DLL or setup</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUsingDownload">In use: the runtime this app hauls aboard.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUsingFile">Usin' {0} from yer file.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterUsingKept">Usin' {0}: the checked copy this app stowed when ye picked it before.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterMissing">{0} be chosen, but there be no copy of it on this vessel yet: choose yer version.dll or setup.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterNeedsAddon">{0} needs add-on v{1} or newer: pick one under Add-on version. Till then the download goes in.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterNeedsOpti">{0} needs OptiScaler {1} or newer: pick one under OptiScaler version. Till then the download goes in.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterNoPatch">The add-on can't run {0} yet: the cargo manifest don't carry its patch. Till it does the download goes in here; the OptiScaler heading runs it as it be.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterKept">Checked an' stowed: danielblnc's runtime {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SupporterRefused">That file be no good. {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Checking">Inspectin' this hold…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.StepDownload">Haul</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.StepVerify">Inspect</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.StepInstall">Hoist</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.StepDone">Arr, done</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Installing">Hoistin'…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Removing">Scuttlin'…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallOk">{0} be rigged. Start the game to use it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallWarn">Hoisted on {0}, with {1} warning to read below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallFail">The hoist on {0} ran aground.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UninstallOk">Scuttled from {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UninstallWarn">Scuttled from {0}, with {1} warning to read below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UninstallFail">Couldn't scuttle everythin' from {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UninstallLeft">{0} still counts as aboard: a file o' this app wouldn't budge. Close the game an' scuttle it again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UninstallClean">Scuttled from {0} — not a plank o' this app left in its hold.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UninstallKeptSettings">Scuttled from {0} — only yer settings stayed: {1}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SettingsLeftTitle">Throw yer settings overboard too?</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SettingsLeftBody">Everythin' this app stowed in {0} be gone. These settings files stayed — they hold what was set in the overlay:</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SettingsRemove">Overboard with 'em</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SettingsRemoveBody">The hold goes back to how it was before the hoist.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SettingsKeep">Keep me settings</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SettingsKeepBody">They stay for the next time ye hoist.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ResultErrors">{0} problem listed below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DownloadFailed">The cargo couldn't be hauled aboard, so nothin' was hoisted.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Folder">Hold</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GameCount">{0} games</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UnknownApi">Mystery API</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Location">Where she lies</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Details">Ship's log</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DetailsCount">{0} lines</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightOk">Ready to hoist</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightOkDetail">Clear seas ahead. Pick a heading below an' press Hoist it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightWarn">Ready to hoist, with {0} note to read</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightErr">{0} problem found in this hold</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightInstalled">Aboard this game</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightInstalledDetail">Start the game to use it. Hoist again to freshen the files, or scuttle to throw 'em out.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightOutdated">Aboard, an' an update be ready</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightOutdatedDetail">The files in this game be older than the ones this app hoists now. Update swaps 'em; yer settings stay.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SeeDetails">Open the Ship's log below to see what was found.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SystemSubtitle">What the add-on needs from this vessel, checked when the app sets sail.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SystemReady">This vessel has what the add-on needs</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SystemNotReady">This vessel be missin' somethin' the add-on needs</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GpuOk">Radeon spotted</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GpuBad">Not a Radeon</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Missing">Lost at sea</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DriverHint">The version Windows reports for the graphics driver.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.FilesHint">Hauled aboard once, checked against a pinned hash, an' reused for every game.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PayloadReadyShort">Checked</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.NotDownloadedShort">Not aboard</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DownloadingShort">Haulin'…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DownloadingPercent">Haulin' {0}%</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SettingsSubtitle">Tongue, updates, an' about this app.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.LanguageHint">Every label switches right away; no need to drop anchor an' restart.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DataFolder">Treasure hold</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.Pcsx2">PCSX2</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.Rpcs3">RPCS3</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.Dx11">D3D10/D3D11 game</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.Dx12">D3D12 game</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.Vulkan">Vulkan game</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.OpenGL">OpenGL game</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.X86Dx11">D3D10/D3D11 game, 32-bit</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.X86Dx9">D3D9 game, 32-bit</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.X86Dx8">D3D8 game, 32-bit</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.X86OpenGL">OpenGL game, 32-bit</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Preset.OptiScaler">OptiScaler: D3D12 game with DLSS, FSR or XeSS</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.Pcsx2">Set the emulator to Direct3D 11: it be the renderer where the network gets the most — the emulator's depth, an' motion from the companion effect when it be aboard. Watch for a per-game override, which beats the global settin' without a word.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.Rpcs3">Experimental. ReShade on Vulkan be a layer, not a proxy DLL: the hoist registers it for yer Windows user an' turns it on for rpcs3.exe with a ReShade.ini. No depth on Vulkan, only colour an' estimated motion.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.Dx11">The finest heading: D3D11 be the only one where the game's own motion vectors reach the network, together with its depth. A D3D10 game sails this heading too, with colour only.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.Dx12">Leaky. On D3D12 the add-on finds the game's depth but not its motion vectors, so the network gets colour an' depth an' guesses the motion. It floats; expect less from it. A game with DLSS, FSR or XeSS in its settings be better served by the OptiScaler heading.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.OptiScaler">Recommended for D3D12 games. Instead o' ReShade this hoists OptiScaler, which commandeers the game's DLSS, FSR or XeSS an' runs the network inside it, with the game's own depth an' motion vectors. The game has to offer one o' those upscalers, switched on in its settings. In game, press Insert, open the Neural tab an' turn on Enable NR; a game with Ray Reconstruction needs "After the finished frame" as the processing point.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.Vulkan">Experimental. ReShade on Vulkan be a layer: the hoist registers it for yer Windows user an' turns it on for this program with a ReShade.ini beside its .exe. There be no depth on Vulkan.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.OpenGL">Experimental. Unlike Vulkan this be an ordinary proxy DLL: ReShade goes aboard as opengl32.dll beside the game, with no separate installer run. Colour an' estimated motion only; the game's own depth be reachable on this API but ain't wired up yet. A 32-bit OpenGL game sails the 32-bit OpenGL heading.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.X86Dx11">Experimental. A 32-bit game can't load the 64-bit runtime, so the add-on sails as a pair sharin' frames on one adapter. Install ReShade with add-on support as the 32-bit dxgi.dll. A D3D10 game sails this heading too, with colour only.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.X86Dx9">Experimental. The same 32-bit pair as D3D11, through a private D3D9/D3D11 stage. Plain D3D9 costs a fixed few milliseconds per frame; D3D9Ex don't. Install ReShade as the 32-bit d3d9.dll.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.X86Dx8">Experimental. D3D8 be translated to D3D9 an' then takes the D3D9 heading above, with the same 32-bit pair. Install ReShade as the 32-bit d3d9.dll.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.X86OpenGL">Experimental. The same 32-bit crew, aboard the game's OpenGL context: colour an' estimated motion only. Put ReShade aboard as the 32-bit opengl32.dll.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PresetNote.FiveM">FiveM has its own anti-cheat: sail at yer own risk, an' check yer server's articles. The add-on an' ReShade go in FiveM.app\plugins, the runtime an' weights beside the game process in data\cache\subprocess. What ye already have in plugins — ReShade.ini, presets, shaders, other add-ons, ENB — stays as it be.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupWelcome">Ahoy!</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupWelcomeBody">The DLSS 5 Neural Rendering network on Radeon cards, through ReShade or OptiScaler. Four quick knots to tie.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupStepMachine">This here vessel</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupStepFiles">Cargo</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupStepGames">Yer plunder</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupBack">Back</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupNext">Onward</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupFinish">Set sail</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupSkip">Skip for now</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupStepOf">Knot {0} o' {1}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupMachineBody">Two things keep the add-on from sailin', an' both be visible from here. Neither one stops ye from carryin' on — only from it workin' inside the game.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupMachineOk">This vessel has everythin' the add-on needs.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupMachineBad">Somethin' be missin'. Ye can carry on an' fix it later, but it won't work in game till ye do.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupFilesBody">The same cargo serves every game: hauled aboard once, checked against a pinned hash, an' reused.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupFilesRetry">Try again</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupFilesLater">Skip this an' the cargo gets hauled on the first hoist.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupGamesBody">Readin' the launchers be look-but-don't-touch: nothin' gets hoisted or changed by lookin'. Ye can add holds by hand afterwards.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupGamesApi">Each game be read to work out which graphics API it uses, an' that readin' be usually right but not always: one hold can carry a D3D11 an' a D3D12 executable, an' a game can default to one API while its executable also supports an older one. Before hoistin', it be worth checkin' the game on pcgamingwiki.com — every game card has a link straight to it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupGamesNone">No games spotted. Ye can add a hold by hand in the main window.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SetupGamesFound">{0} games spotted.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Unexpected">Blow me down, somethin' unexpected happened. The whole ship's log was written.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Play">Set sail</sys:String>
