  <sys:String x:Key="Str.AddMenuEmulator">An emulator…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UpdateShort">Update</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GamesAway">{0} on a drive that's out at sea</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GamesAwayHint">Games on a drive that ain't plugged in right now stay remembered, with everythin' chosen for 'em, an' come back when the drive makes port.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GameGone">{0} ain't aboard no more, so it left the list.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GamesGone">{0} game ain't aboard no more, so it left the list.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GamesGone.Many">{0} games ain't aboard no more, so they left the list.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ShowDetails">Show the ship's log</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DetectedSection">Spotted</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallsInto">Stowed in: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallsElsewhere">This be outside the folder ye added: 'tis where {0} lies, the build the launcher sets sail. If ye play another build, choose its {0} above.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.CheckApiTip">Files say what a game links against, not what it sails on: one hold can carry a D3D11 an' a D3D12 executable. The wiki says which the game uses.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DetectedFromFiles">Read from the game's own files.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DetectedFromWiki">From PCGamingWiki an' the game's files.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallWith">Hoist with</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteReShade">ReShade + add-on</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteOpti">OptiScaler</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Recommended">Cap'n's pick</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RecommendedLower">cap'n's pick</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteReShadeSummary">The add-on inside ReShade. D3D11, D3D12, Vulkan, OpenGL, 32-bit games an' emulators.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteReShadeMisfit">No ReShade heading for what this game reads as ({0}).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteOptiSummary">Sails inside the game's DLSS, FSR or XeSS, with its own depth an' motion. Replaces ReShade.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteOptiFound">Sails inside the game's upscaler ({0} spotted here). Replaces ReShade.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.RouteOptiMisfit">Made for 64-bit D3D12 games; this one reads as {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ApiSection">Graphics API</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Group64">64-bit games</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Group32">32-bit games (experimental)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GroupEmulators">Emulators</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.GroupFiveM">GTA V online</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.OptiAbout">Instead o' ReShade this hoists OptiScaler, which commandeers the game's DLSS, FSR or XeSS an' runs the network inside it, with the game's own depth an' motion vectors.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InGame">In the game</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.OptiStep1">Turn on DLSS, FSR or XeSS in the game's graphics settings.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.OptiStep2">Press Insert, open the Neural tab an' turn on Enable NR.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.OptiStep3">With Ray Reconstruction on, set the processing point to "After the finished frame".</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallOpti">Hoist OptiScaler</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Update">Update</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Reinstall">Hoist again</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchToOpti">Change course to OptiScaler</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchToReShade">Change course to ReShade</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchTitle">Change course to {0}?</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchBody">{0} has the {1} heading aboard, an' the two can't share one hold. {1} gets scuttled first, puttin' back anythin' it replaced, an' then {2} gets hoisted.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchYes">Scuttle {0}, hoist {1}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchYesBody">Yer own settings files stay right where they be.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.SwitchNoBody">Nothin' changes; {0} stays aboard.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DownloadFailedDetail">Why be in the Ship's log. Nothin' was hoisted.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DownloadFailedHelp">The cargo can also be fetched with a browser an' handed over: This here vessel &gt; Cargo &gt; Haul by hand, then Import cargo. Files in yer Downloads folder be found on their own.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DnsRetry">Swab the DNS an' try again</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DnsFlushFailed">Windows wouldn't swab its DNS cache from here. Open a Command Prompt, run ipconfig /flushdns, an' try again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightErr.Many">{0} problems found in this hold</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PreflightWarn.Many">Ready to hoist, with {0} notes to read</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.InstallWarn.Many">Hoisted on {0}, with {1} warnings to read below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.UninstallWarn.Many">Scuttled from {0}, with {1} warnings to read below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ResultErrors.Many">{0} problems listed below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManifestFailedShort">No cargo manifest</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.FailedShort">Sunk</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PayloadsAllReadyShort">All {0} aboard</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.PayloadsMissingShort">{0} lost at sea · {1}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.DownloadFailedOne">Couldn't haul: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManualDownload">Haul by hand</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ImportFiles">Import cargo…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ImportHint">Pick a hold with files ye hauled yerself. Each one be known by its name an' taken only if it matches its pinned hash.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManualTitle">Haul the cargo yerself</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ManualBody">Open each link in a browser an' save the file anywhere: the Downloads folder be searched on its own, an' Import cargo takes any other hold. Names don't need changin', an' nothin' that don't match its pinned SHA-256 gets used.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ImportPick">Pick the hold with the files ye hauled</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ImportAll">Every file be aboard now an' checked.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ImportNothing">Nothin' in that hold matched a file this needs.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.ImportSome">Taken: {0}. Still lost at sea: {1}.</sys:String>
