  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Transfer">NR settings</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferTip">This game's NR settings in one file, to stow or to share, an' the way to bring aboard someone else's. Close the game first: it stows its settings when it exits.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferExport">Export to a file…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferImport">Import from a file…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferNothing">Nothin' to export yet: the settings get written the first time the game sails with the mod.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferExported">Settings stowed in {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferImported">The settings from {0} be aboard. The ones they replaced were stowed in {1}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferWrongRoute">These settings be for the {0} heading, an' this game has {1} aboard.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.TransferInvalid">That file ain't an AMD-NR settings export.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.pcsx2">Settings &gt; Graphics &gt; Renderer: Direct3D 11. Watch for a per-game override in the game properties — it beats the global settin' without a word, an' it be the most common way this looks broken when it ain't.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.rpcs3">Settings &gt; GPU &gt; Renderer: Vulkan. There be no Direct3D here at all, so this heading gets colour an' estimated motion only — no depth.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.duckstation">Settings &gt; Graphics &gt; Renderer: Direct3D 11.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.dolphin">Graphics &gt; General &gt; Backend: Direct3D 11.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.ppsspp">Settings &gt; Graphics &gt; Backend: Direct3D 11.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.flycast">Settings &gt; Graphics &gt; Graphics API: DirectX 11.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.xenia">It sails on D3D12, which be the leaky heading: the add-on be shown the finished frame an' nothin' else. It floats; expect less from it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.cemu">Options &gt; General settings &gt; Graphics &gt; Graphics API: Vulkan. No depth on Vulkan: colour an' estimated motion only.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.ryujinx">Options &gt; Settings &gt; Graphics &gt; Graphics Backend: Vulkan. No depth on Vulkan.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.yuzu">Emulation &gt; Configure &gt; Graphics &gt; API: Vulkan. No depth on Vulkan.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.vita3k">Vulkan be the default backend. No depth on Vulkan.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.shadps4">Vulkan only. No depth on Vulkan, an' this emulator be a young ship itself — expect rough seas.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.kyty">Vulkan only. Point at kyty_emulator.exe's folder (launcher.exe only starts it). No depth, an' the emulator be young yet — expect squalls.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.fivem">In game: Home opens ReShade, an' AMD Neural Rendering be under Add-ons, or Ctrl+End. FiveM has its own anti-cheat — check yer server's articles first.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.azahar">Emulation &gt; Configure &gt; Graphics &gt; Graphics API: Vulkan. OpenGL has a heading now too, but Vulkan be the one with the nautical miles on it here.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.xemu">xemu renders with OpenGL an' nothin' else, so the OpenGL heading be the only one there is here. It be the newest o' the headings an' it be experimental: colour an' estimated motion, no depth.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Str.Emulator.melonds">Emu settings &gt; Video &gt; 3D renderer: OpenGL. The software renderer draws on the CPU an' there be nothin' there for an add-on to grab, so it has to be the OpenGL one — an' that heading be experimental: colour an' estimated motion, no depth.</sys:String>

</ResourceDictionary>
